Alternatively, maybe the services are not yet deployed, but the user mentioned the application is running. So, checking the actual Kubernetes resources makes sense. Once the services are identified, the next steps could involve checking their pods, deployments, metrics, and dependencies. So, using kubectl to get services is a logical next step to gather that information.
