ceed. The initial step would be to get the dependency graph to see if there are any services with high latency or failed calls. If the dependency graph shows something wrong, then the next step would be to check traces for those specific services. \n\nSo, the next logical step is to use get_dependency_graph with a reasonable time frame, like the last 10 minutes, to capture any recent issues. This would help identify if there are any services that are having trouble communicating with others, which could be the root cause.\n</think>\n\nget_dependency_graph  \nThe `get_metrics` query returned no error data, suggesting HTTP-level issues may not be the problem. To identify potential communication failures between microservices, I will retrieve the service dependency graph from Jaeger. This will reveal latency spikes, failed calls, or missing dependencies that could indicate root causes like network issues, misconfigurations, or cascading failures.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_dependency_graph", "arguments": {"last_n_minutes": 10}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=494, prompt_tokens=2591, total_tokens=3085, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfaef-d6ac-7492-90bb-ae2dfd54c441-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2591, 'output_tokens': 494, 'total_tokens': 3085}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='dd5a1438-7659-4ee7-97b3-6ca197ebc99e')]]
