rors didn\'t return any data, which might mean that the application isn\'t generating those metrics, or the query is incorrect. Maybe the user should check the Prometheus query again to ensure it\'s correctly capturing the relevant metrics. But since the user is focusing on traces and dependencies, maybe the next step is to look into the dependency graph to see if there are any unexpected patterns or failures in the service interactions.\n</think>\n\nget_dependency_graph  \nThe traces for the `frontend` service show normal HTTP responses, but there might be underlying issues in service dependencies (e.g., latency, failed calls, or missing dependencies). Retrieving the dependency graph from Jaeger will reveal relationships and potential bottlenecks between services, such as unexpected delays or failed communication paths. This will help identify root causes like network issues, misconfigurations, or cascading failures.  \n\n<tool_call>\n{"name": "get_dependency_graph", "arguments": {"last_n_minutes": 10}}\n</tool_call>', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=534, prompt_tokens=9581, total_tokens=10115, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfaf0-040e-7ff3-a38d-eb1a9bae4f10-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9581, 'output_tokens': 534, 'total_tokens': 10115}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='49086027-4ac3-4c31-841d-4a24e2c582f8')]]
